# Site-level log policy for the Majadu handler on api.qouver.com.
#
# The share code and the one-use websocket ticket are query parameters, and this
# access log is shared with every other application on the site, so a matcher
# that names only /majadu/s/* writes live tickets into a file that outlives the
# link. Both prefixes are required and cutover.sh refuses a Caddyfile that names
# one of them.
#
# Install (cutover.sh does this) as:
#   /srv/qouver/apps/majadu/caddy/log-share.caddy
#
# then replace the bare `log` statement of the api.qouver.com site block with:
#   import /srv/qouver/apps/majadu/caddy/log-share.caddy
#
# `skip_log` needs Caddy 2.7+. `log_access` is the host's existing output and
# format snippet; keep its name so the other applications log unchanged.
@share path /majadu/s/* /majadu/ws/*
log {
	import log_access
	skip_log @share
}
